    "description": "The ProTerra is the 50-gallon tank for an electric home where the space allows it. A heat pump on top of the tank pulls heat out of the surrounding air and pushes it into the water, and Rheem lists the XE50T10HS45U1 at a 3.88 UEF, against 0.93 for a standard electric tank. On the estimate in our running-cost section, that cuts a typical family's electric water-heating bill by roughly three quarters. It also carries the longest warranty on this page, ten years on the tank and parts, and adds LeakGuard, which senses a leak and closes a shutoff valve, plus Wi-Fi control through Rheem's app. The catches are physical. Rheem lists it at about 78-5/8 inches tall and 25-3/8 inches wide, around 30 inches taller than the medium electric above, and the heat pump needs a good volume of surrounding air or a louvered door to work well. It cools the room it sits in, which is welcome in a hot garage and less welcome in a small basement in January, and it needs a condensate drain. Our <a href=\"/best-heat-pump-water-heater/\">heat pump water heater guide</a> compares it against the other hybrids."
