          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is a 50 gallon hybrid water heater worth it?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "In an all-electric home with enough space, usually yes. Rated at around 3.9 UEF against 0.93 for a standard electric tank, a hybrid can cut the electric water-heating bill by roughly three quarters, and rebates and tax credits often cover much of the price difference. It is not worth it where it will not fit, in a small closed closet, or in a home already on cheap natural gas."
          }
